import torch, torch.nn.functional as F

def dro_gap(samples_w, samples_l, c):
    """samples_*: [K,M] reward samples per candidate"""
    q_w = torch.quantile(samples_w, c, dim=-1)
    q_l = torch.quantile(samples_l, 1-c, dim=-1)
    worst_dim = (q_w - q_l).max(dim=0).values  # shape [K] -> scalar per pair via max
    return worst_dim  # Δ̃

class DROIDPO(torch.nn.Module):
    def __init__(self, model, beta=0.1, c_max=0.2):
        super().__init__(); self.model=model; self.beta=beta; self.c_max=c_max
    def loss(self, batch, step, total):
        c = self.c_max*step/total
        gap = dro_gap(batch['samples_w'], batch['samples_l'], c)  # [B]
        logits = self.beta*gap + batch['logp_w'] - batch['logp_l']
        return F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(logits, torch.ones_like(logits))

evaluate.novelty_reason:
The literature already contains (1) offline preference-learning objectives that optimise the mean reward (DPO, GDPO, DiscoPOP, KTO), (2) CVaR-style risk-aware objectives, but only in an on-policy RLHF setting (RA-RLHF) or in an offline setting that assumes Gaussian rewards and a fixed risk level (CVaR-DPO), and (3) soft-label / uncertainty-aware variants that do not consider tail-risk (GDPO, Geometric-DPO).  The proposed DRO-DPO is the first to combine the following elements in a single, fully-offline loss:
• non-parametric CVaR estimation via empirical quantiles, removing the normality assumption;
• explicit distributional-robustness to heavy-tailed or skewed reward posteriors proven with a Bernstein–Catoni bound;
• automatic annealing of the risk level c (no τ grid-search) embedded inside the loss;
• simultaneous handling of multiple heterogeneous safety rewards without extra hyper-parameters (max-over-heads trick);
• practical implementation that only adds quantile() operations to the standard DPO pipeline.
None of the surveyed related works covers this particular intersection of risk-aversion, uncertainty calibration, multi-objective safety, and offline efficiency, therefore the method has clear incremental but real novelty.

